Shader compile: hand vitaShaRK the source length (fix of the Strikers port's change)

shark_compile_shader_extended's size argument is in/out: it reads the
source length from it (input.size = *size, checked in the disassembly of
libvitashark.a) and writes the program size back. The Strikers code passed
a zeroed candidate.size so as not to clobber s->size, which handed the
compiler an empty source (in Vita3K: 13 'fatal internal error' compiles in
a 400 s Gateway run that the old code never shows). The candidate now
starts with the source length; s->size is still left alone.
---
 source/custom_shaders.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/custom_shaders.c b/source/custom_shaders.c
index 723b583..1419be6 100644
--- a/source/custom_shaders.c
+++ b/source/custom_shaders.c
@@ -810,6 +810,9 @@ static inline __attribute__((always_inline)) void compile_shader(shader *s, GLbo
 		return;
 	shader candidate = {0};
 	// The compiler owns its output. Do not publish it or clobber the source length.
+	// (galaxy: the size argument is in/out: vitaShaRK reads the SOURCE length from it (shark_input.size = *size) and writes
+	// the program size back. The Strikers port passed 0 here, so the compiler was handed an empty source.)
+	candidate.size = s->size;
 	const SceGxmProgram *output = shark_compile_shader_extended((const char *)s->source, &candidate.size, s->type == GL_FRAGMENT_SHADER ? SHARK_FRAGMENT_SHADER : SHARK_VERTEX_SHADER, compiler_opts, compiler_fastmath, compiler_fastprecision, compiler_fastint);
 	if (output && candidate.size) {
 		SceGxmProgram *res = (SceGxmProgram *)vglMalloc(candidate.size);
